# README — DeepWiki badge

The **root `README.md`** must include the **Ask DeepWiki** badge next to the other top badges (same block under the title / centered intro).

## Required markup

Use this exact link target (repository: `hrodrig/pgwd`). Only change it if the GitHub org/repo or DeepWiki URL changes.

```markdown
[![Ask DeepWiki](https://deepwiki.com/badge.svg)](https://deepwiki.com/hrodrig/pgwd)
```

## When to verify

- After editing the badge row in `README.md`.
- Before release or when preparing README-only PRs: confirm the line is present and the link opens the correct DeepWiki page.

## Generator

Optional: [DeepWiki Badge Maker](https://deepwiki.com/badge-maker) can regenerate the snippet if the canonical URL changes.

Do not remove this badge without replacing it with an equivalent link to up-to-date, repo-specific documentation (DeepWiki or agreed successor).
